    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a bit of a mystery to me. I never really liked it in school, and even though I work with computers, I'm not naturally inclined toward complex equations. My father was a PhD, and he made me think it was something we could all do, but I always felt it demanded a different way of thinking than I was comfortable with. It's a subject I appreciate in broad strokes, like a language, but not in the detail.",
